@@ -12,6 +12,9 @@ The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/),
 - OpenRouter cost journal: each attempt of an OpenRouter job appends one JSON line to `<state>/openrouter-costs.jsonl` (mode 600, append-only; written on success, failure, budget refusal and on the daemon's SIGTERM) with its tokens, the proxy's cost and OpenRouter's billed record of its generations (`GET /api/v1/generation`, read by the wrapper with the key, which never reaches the line); `agent-jobs openrouter costs --agent A [--days N] [--json] [--reconcile]` lists the runs with both costs (a mismatch over 10% flagged), totals per day, per model and over 30 days, the key's usage and limit (`GET /api/v1/key`), and fills missing OpenRouter records by appending reconcile lines. The proxy removes the key and anything `sk-or-` shaped from upstream error bodies (non-200, forwarded with their own Content-Length) and from a stream's error events before claude sees them.
 - `job_start sources` (#125) accepts up to 10 absolute file paths or `job:<id>` reports of the same agent, at most 2 MiB per regular file. It snapshots them read-only into `sources/` before enqueue and lists their origins in the prompt; CLI `start --source` is repeatable, symlinks are refused, and repository cloning stays disabled.
 
+### Security
+- The orchestrator no longer runs job-controlled code for the browser check (#135). New `agent-jobs ui-check <base-url> <path>... [--playwright <path>]` writes the `scripts/ui-check.mjs` embedded in the binary to a private temp dir and runs it with `--trusted`; prompts/orchestrator.md and the skill name it instead of `<job dir>/tools/ui-check.mjs`, which the job can rewrite. The script's new `--trusted` never resolves Playwright from the current directory (a job worktree's planted `node_modules/playwright`) or from relative `NODE_PATH` entries, and `--playwright <path>` names the module explicitly (absolute under `--trusted`); `npm root -g` runs in the script's own directory, and the command drops `NODE_OPTIONS` and relative `NODE_PATH` entries from node's environment. Jobs keep running their own `tools/ui-check.mjs` as before.
+
 ### Docs
 - What a job cannot do (ssh and other out-of-scope tools, anything outside, other jobs' state) and where that work goes instead: a subagent in the orchestrator's session with a short summary, bulky data handed to the job as a file on a local `base` branch, decided before `job_start` (skills/agent-jobs/SKILL.md, docs/GUIDE.md).
 
